# Walkthrough: Relocated Sync Status Indicator

I have relocated the Canvas synchronization status indicator from the sidebar to the dashboard header and updated its design to be more subtle and consistent with the dashboard's status badges.

## Changes Made

### 1. Refactored Sync Status Indicator
- [SyncStatusIndicator.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/dashboard/SyncStatusIndicator.tsx) was redesigned to look like a badge rather than a card.
- It now uses a subtle color scheme based on the sync status (Success, Running, or Error).
- The layout is now more horizontal and compact, displaying "Synced", "Syncing", or "Error" along with the relative time.

### 2. Sidebar Cleanup
- [Sidebar.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx) no longer contains the sync status indicator.
- The vertical space is now cleaner, focusing on navigation and user settings.

### 3. Dashboard Integration
- [DashboardHeader.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/dashboard/DashboardHeader.tsx) now includes the [SyncStatusIndicator](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/dashboard/SyncStatusIndicator.tsx#8-74) next to the numerical stats (tasks, classes, etc.).
- It aligns perfectly with the other "StatBadges", providing a unified "at-a-glance" status area.

## Verification
- Verified that the [SyncStatusIndicator](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/dashboard/SyncStatusIndicator.tsx#8-74) is correctly imported and rendered in the [DashboardHeader](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/dashboard/DashboardHeader.tsx#42-178).
- Confirmed that the [Sidebar](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx#56-207) is properly updated.
- The new badge design handles "Synced" (emerald), "Syncing" (accent animate-spin), and "Error" (urgency) states correctly.
